      "kind": "teaching_action_meta",
      "conceptId": "math.prob.quantile",
      "title": "PARTIAL (confuses Q and F) → \"F maps VALUES to PROBABILITIES: F(x)=P(X≤x). Q maps PROBABILITIES to VALUES: Q(p)=inf{x:F(x)≥p}. They are inverses of each other (when F is invertible). Example: if F(3)=0.7, then Q(0.7)=3.\" → TB-R01 → Gate",
      "content": "{\"id\":\"TA-12\",\"title\":\"PARTIAL (confuses Q and F) → \\\"F maps VALUES to PROBABILITIES: F(x)=P(X≤x). Q maps PROBABILITIES to VALUES: Q(p)=inf{x:F(x)≥p}. They are inverses of each other (when F is invertible). Example: if F(3)=0.7, then Q(0.7)=3.\\\" → TB-R01 → Gate\",\"primitives\":[],\"addresses\":[]}",
